       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. A sertraline dose of 1000 mg once daily is far outside the normal range. The labeled maximum is 200 mg per day, and the usual adult range is 50 to 200 mg. Taking that dose could cause serious harm, such as serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, or seizures.\n\nIt may be a typo, such as 100 mg or 50 mg, or a unit mix-up. It may also have been meant for a different drug.\n\nBecause you're not a clinician, this order also needs to come from the treating prescriber. Please contact the medicine team and the pharmacist to verify the intended drug, dose, and frequency. If a clinician confirms a dose after reviewing the patient's situation, they can enter it directly, or send me the verified details and I can enter them."
